  "id": "osf-builder-attribution-and-diff-anchoring",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-11T14:38:41.975Z",
  "title": "Builder attribution fails closed; findings anchor to the PR diff",
  "summary": "This change makes two parts of `osf review run` stricter and more resilient. Builder-family detection now reads every word of a `Code-Generator:` trailer (vendor names and model ids alike), reports per-commit reasons when a family cannot be told apart, and fails the run closed as could-not-run when any commit's family is unknown — except a clean merge that introduces nothing of its own, which `git merge-tree --write-tree` proves against a scratch object store so a read-only checkout still works. On the posting side, findings are now checked against the pull request's actual diff: only lines GitHub shows on the new side become inline comments, everything else moves into the review body under a heading, and a body that would exceed the limit is cut and counted rather than refused, so a review always posts.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
